    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the file's established conventions cleanly:\n\n- `getMembershipLevel()` continues the same `@Transient`-derived-getter pattern used throughout `Owner` (`getAgeBand`, `getCheckDigit`, `getIdentityKey`), and the new household gain reads exactly like the existing email and namesake increments.\n- The tenure logic is extracted into a private `hasTenureForLevel4()` helper rather than inlined into the already-growing getter, which keeps the main method readable and gives the rule a self-documenting name. This is the natural place for it \u2014 a derived property of the domain object lives on the domain object.\n- The null-guard style (`registrationDate == null`) mirrors the existing null handling in `getAgeBand`/`getCheckDigit`, and `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(...)` is the idiomatic choice alongside the existing `Period`/`LocalDate` usage.\n- The Javadoc was updated to match the new behavior (level range, the household gain, and the tenure cap), and the helper carries its own focused doc comment.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all accumulation, logic sits in the right unit \u2014 a maintainer of this codebase would find this natural.",
